1
00:00:11,011 --> 00:00:13,013
[♪ opening theme music playing]

2
00:00:38,413 --> 00:00:40,666
THE REMARRIED EMPRESS

3
00:00:46,129 --> 00:00:48,131
[♪ melancholy music playing]

4
00:01:05,315 --> 00:01:06,400
[horse snorts softly]

5
00:01:11,947 --> 00:01:12,948
[sighs softly]

6
00:01:22,583 --> 00:01:23,917
Let's go.

7
00:01:27,379 --> 00:01:28,797
[horse whinnies]

8
00:01:37,639 --> 00:01:39,600
[♪ music continues]

9
00:01:59,911 --> 00:02:01,204
[♪ music fades]

10
00:02:01,288 --> 00:02:02,914
[♪ dramatic music playing]

11
00:02:11,298 --> 00:02:12,591
-[♪ music swells]
-[birds chirping]

12
00:02:12,674 --> 00:02:16,386
WESTERN KINGDOM

13
00:02:29,316 --> 00:02:30,359
[♪ music fades]

14
00:02:32,736 --> 00:02:34,029
[♪ moody music playing]

15
00:02:34,112 --> 00:02:36,114
[breathing heavily]

16
00:02:40,869 --> 00:02:41,912
[door opens]

17
00:02:41,995 --> 00:02:43,080
[continues breathing heavily]

18
00:02:44,831 --> 00:02:45,999
[door closes]

19
00:02:46,083 --> 00:02:47,501
[footsteps approaching]

20
00:03:03,100 --> 00:03:04,309
[sighs heavily]

21
00:03:07,312 --> 00:03:08,355
My king.

22
00:03:17,906 --> 00:03:19,908
[♪ dramatic music playing]

23
00:03:26,373 --> 00:03:27,457
You have returned.

24
00:03:28,750 --> 00:03:30,585
[breathing heavily]

25
00:03:40,011 --> 00:03:41,012
[♪ music fades]

26
00:03:43,849 --> 00:03:45,517
[♪ moody music playing]

27
00:03:51,731 --> 00:03:53,316
You look well, Your Majesty.

28
00:03:56,069 --> 00:03:57,070
Heinrey…

29
00:03:58,405 --> 00:03:59,614
Have you forgotten?

30
00:04:01,324 --> 00:04:03,952
The green emeralds
embedded in the red walls

31
00:04:04,619 --> 00:04:05,871
of our hometown.

32
00:04:06,580 --> 00:04:08,039
[wind whooshing]

33
00:04:09,207 --> 00:04:10,792
We can never return there.

34
00:04:15,797 --> 00:04:17,382
Yet, I still see it clearly.

35
00:04:23,346 --> 00:04:25,390
It was the capital of the Western Kingdom.

36
00:04:36,318 --> 00:04:38,153
-[sword swooshes]
-[squelches]

37
00:04:45,869 --> 00:04:47,704
[Walton III] <i>When the crown</i>
<i>was first laid upon my head,</i>

38
00:04:47,788 --> 00:04:50,207
<i>I resolved that</i>
<i>I would ride in no carriage</i>

39
00:04:50,290 --> 00:04:52,334
<i>until the harbor was ours once again.</i>

40
00:04:52,417 --> 00:04:54,836
Until it was won from the Eastern Empire.

41
00:04:55,796 --> 00:04:57,714
We will reclaim it in a single breath

42
00:04:58,298 --> 00:04:59,758
once your health is regained.

43
00:05:00,467 --> 00:05:01,468
Heinrey…

44
00:05:07,808 --> 00:05:09,059
Soon…

45
00:05:11,228 --> 00:05:12,729
you will inherit the throne.

46
00:05:14,606 --> 00:05:15,941
Our kingdom…

47
00:05:16,566 --> 00:05:20,320
It remained strong all this time,
thanks to the queen's family.

48
00:05:21,404 --> 00:05:23,240
If their support were to end…

49
00:05:24,282 --> 00:05:26,201
then our nation will fall into disarray.

50
00:05:26,284 --> 00:05:28,578
You will need to continue this alliance.

51
00:05:29,329 --> 00:05:30,330
Do you hear me?

52
00:05:35,877 --> 00:05:37,003
Queen Krista…

53
00:05:37,963 --> 00:05:39,631
You may have to wed her to do so.

54
00:05:50,308 --> 00:05:53,103
I apologize for taking her from you
when we were young.

55
00:05:53,186 --> 00:05:54,312
She was my fate.

56
00:05:56,273 --> 00:05:57,274
I had dreamt…

57
00:05:58,191 --> 00:06:00,235
Dreamt of reclaiming the harbor.

58
00:06:00,819 --> 00:06:02,070
And that I would see you rise.

59
00:06:02,737 --> 00:06:04,698
Rise to our kingdom's throne willingly.

60
00:06:07,742 --> 00:06:08,869
That is not the case.

61
00:06:09,744 --> 00:06:10,787
I am so sorry.

62
00:06:11,580 --> 00:06:13,790
It is only pain you have inherited.

63
00:06:14,541 --> 00:06:15,542
My king.

64
00:06:16,084 --> 00:06:17,085
Heinrey.

65
00:06:20,964 --> 00:06:22,674
My dearest Heinrey.

66
00:06:22,757 --> 00:06:24,509
[♪ soft music playing]

67
00:06:24,593 --> 00:06:26,428
I will always be your older brother.

68
00:06:28,638 --> 00:06:29,890
[Heinrey sighs]

69
00:06:30,724 --> 00:06:32,058
[sniffling softly]

70
00:06:34,144 --> 00:06:35,645
[breath trembling]

71
00:06:35,729 --> 00:06:36,938
Yes.

72
00:06:37,522 --> 00:06:38,690
Know this.

73
00:06:38,773 --> 00:06:40,108
I will watch over you.

74
00:06:43,737 --> 00:06:45,780
I will stay at your side forever.

75
00:06:47,240 --> 00:06:48,909
[Heinrey sobs softly]

76
00:07:16,436 --> 00:07:17,646
[thunder rumbling]

77
00:07:31,826 --> 00:07:34,287
[Sovieshu] As Walton III
has departed this world,

78
00:07:34,871 --> 00:07:37,582
my heart aches
as though I've lost an old friend.

79
00:07:39,626 --> 00:07:42,921
I wish you to know that
the Eastern Empire shares in the sorrow

80
00:07:43,004 --> 00:07:45,090
of the people of the Western Kingdom.

81
00:07:45,173 --> 00:07:49,302
I will be sure to convey Your Majesty's
gracious and thoughtful words of comfort

82
00:07:49,386 --> 00:07:50,428
to King Heinrey.

83
00:07:50,512 --> 00:07:52,597
The King's succession.

84
00:07:52,681 --> 00:07:54,015
I trust it is all going well?

85
00:07:54,099 --> 00:07:56,434
Prince Heinrey,
the younger brother of Walton III,

86
00:07:56,518 --> 00:07:57,519
has ascended the throne

87
00:07:57,602 --> 00:08:00,563
and is overseeing the preparations
for the funeral and coronation.

88
00:08:01,481 --> 00:08:03,942
King of the West, Heinrey,

89
00:08:04,025 --> 00:08:05,985
I offer my… sincere blessings.

90
00:08:12,117 --> 00:08:13,952
So Heinrey is king now.

91
00:08:14,035 --> 00:08:15,662
[Foreign Minister]
This man left the royal court,

92
00:08:15,745 --> 00:08:18,164
wandered all his life
and was distant from politics.

93
00:08:18,248 --> 00:08:22,085
Even if he inherits the throne,
he will be manipulated by the nobles.

94
00:08:24,003 --> 00:08:26,256
What news of the Western Elder Council?

95
00:08:26,339 --> 00:08:27,549
Is their influence still strong?

96
00:08:27,632 --> 00:08:29,592
Duke Zemensia,
who controls the Council of Elders,

97
00:08:29,676 --> 00:08:31,469
shared power with the late king.

98
00:08:32,053 --> 00:08:34,055
But has not revealed
what kind of new relationship

99
00:08:34,139 --> 00:08:35,515
he will demand from King Heinrey.

100
00:08:35,598 --> 00:08:39,018
I fear we'll see turmoil
before the new power even settles.

101
00:08:39,102 --> 00:08:40,645
[Sovieshu]
He will not be easy to deal with.

102
00:08:40,729 --> 00:08:42,897
He is a crude and sly individual.

103
00:08:43,773 --> 00:08:45,650
What do you think?

104
00:08:46,526 --> 00:08:48,153
The two of you were…

105
00:08:49,279 --> 00:08:50,697
quite close in the end.

106
00:08:53,408 --> 00:08:57,120
This coronation will bring together
delegates of many nations.

107
00:08:57,203 --> 00:08:58,747
For the prestige of the Eastern Empire,

108
00:08:58,830 --> 00:09:01,249
I would advise
that we select ours suitably.

109
00:09:03,334 --> 00:09:06,546
Confer with the Foreign Minister
and arrange a proper delegation.

110
00:09:09,424 --> 00:09:10,717
Ah…

111
00:09:11,718 --> 00:09:13,970
Rashta's pregnancy celebration…

112
00:09:16,097 --> 00:09:17,182
I suppose…

113
00:09:19,059 --> 00:09:20,351
you will not attend?

114
00:09:21,478 --> 00:09:22,562
[Sovieshu scoffs]

115
00:09:23,063 --> 00:09:25,190
I would imagine that this is a good thing.

116
00:09:25,899 --> 00:09:29,069
The noble ladies wish
to gather and celebrate this child

117
00:09:29,152 --> 00:09:30,653
and they may feel uncomfortable…

118
00:09:32,363 --> 00:09:34,115
being mindful of you.

119
00:09:45,543 --> 00:09:50,507
Uh, so when do you plan
to lift the banishment on Sir Kosair?

120
00:09:50,590 --> 00:09:51,883
Or is he still forbidden?

121
00:09:52,592 --> 00:09:54,469
That depends on Rashta's condition.

122
00:09:54,552 --> 00:09:56,429
If she worsens, and she may,

123
00:09:56,513 --> 00:09:57,931
he must handle the consequences.

124
00:09:58,014 --> 00:10:00,308
I do not take this decision lightly.

125
00:10:02,310 --> 00:10:04,312
[♪ soft, mysterious music playing]

126
00:10:26,292 --> 00:10:28,086
I asked Annie to spy, Your Majesty.

127
00:10:28,670 --> 00:10:31,172
She was to gain information
from the Rose Room.

128
00:10:31,256 --> 00:10:34,843
Sir Artina noticed someone suspicious
kept visiting Ms. Rashta,

129
00:10:34,926 --> 00:10:36,302
so I wanted to find out more.

130
00:10:37,387 --> 00:10:38,596
Visiting Rashta?

131
00:10:39,597 --> 00:10:42,433
-Who was it?
-Ms. Rashta's old master.

132
00:10:42,517 --> 00:10:43,768
Lotteshu, Your Majesty.

133
00:10:45,145 --> 00:10:46,896
And that man has been here?

134
00:10:47,480 --> 00:10:49,566
-His Majesty, is he aware?
-It does not seem so.

135
00:10:49,649 --> 00:10:51,359
[Eliza] That is not all, Your Majesty.

136
00:10:51,442 --> 00:10:52,777
It concerns Rashta.

137
00:10:53,361 --> 00:10:54,404
She has been…

138
00:10:54,487 --> 00:10:56,072
extorted for money by that man.

139
00:10:56,156 --> 00:10:58,616
[♪ ominous music playing]

140
00:10:58,700 --> 00:10:59,742
[coins clinking]

141
00:11:01,035 --> 00:11:02,704
This is the last time, all right?

142
00:11:03,621 --> 00:11:04,664
I have nothing else.

143
00:11:13,923 --> 00:11:15,008
[Rashta grunts in pain]

144
00:11:18,386 --> 00:11:21,014
[Navier] <i>He must have something</i>
<i>he is using against her.</i>

145
00:11:21,097 --> 00:11:22,765
[Eliza] <i>That is also my assumption.</i>

146
00:11:24,350 --> 00:11:25,977
But what could he be holding over her?

147
00:11:28,313 --> 00:11:29,981
Hard to say.

148
00:11:30,064 --> 00:11:32,692
I heard he only recently
moved to the capital.

149
00:11:35,653 --> 00:11:37,488
If you command it,

150
00:11:37,572 --> 00:11:40,033
I will investigate
Viscount Lotteshu's movements.

151
00:11:40,116 --> 00:11:42,243
[♪ music continues]

152
00:11:47,957 --> 00:11:49,125
[women chuckle softly]

153
00:11:52,170 --> 00:11:53,588
[♪ music fades]

154
00:11:53,671 --> 00:11:55,215
[Albani] Good heavens!

155
00:11:55,840 --> 00:11:58,927
They say, since the New Year,
this is the biggest party they've seen.

156
00:11:59,010 --> 00:12:00,386
[Albani chuckles]

157
00:12:03,473 --> 00:12:05,808
[♪ gentle music playing]

158
00:12:07,060 --> 00:12:08,102
[Rashta] <i>My baby,</i>

159
00:12:08,811 --> 00:12:10,563
<i>do you hear the commotion outside?</i>

160
00:12:11,648 --> 00:12:14,901
<i>Those arrogant nobles</i>
<i>have all come here to see you.</i>

161
00:12:15,485 --> 00:12:17,862
<i>The people who despised me</i>
<i>as a lowly slave</i>

162
00:12:17,946 --> 00:12:21,616
<i>are now lining up,</i>
<i>holding treasures of gold and silver,</i>

163
00:12:21,699 --> 00:12:22,992
<i>trying to win your favor.</i>

164
00:12:24,369 --> 00:12:28,414
<i>Those same people</i>
<i>will all be bowing at your feet one day.</i>

165
00:12:28,498 --> 00:12:29,958
[Albani sighs, clears throat]

166
00:12:32,919 --> 00:12:33,920
[Rashta gasps]

167
00:12:37,340 --> 00:12:38,341
[Albani] Mmm.

168
00:12:40,885 --> 00:12:42,095
Your Majesty.

169
00:12:45,181 --> 00:12:46,599
Are you not tired?

170
00:12:47,100 --> 00:12:48,685
I am quite well.

171
00:12:56,109 --> 00:12:57,527
Where's the ring?

172
00:12:57,610 --> 00:12:58,611
The ring?

173
00:12:59,153 --> 00:13:00,154
Yes.

174
00:13:00,238 --> 00:13:02,782
I'm talking about the Crimson Ring.

175
00:13:11,958 --> 00:13:13,543
[♪ ominous music playing]

176
00:13:16,963 --> 00:13:18,339
Ah…

177
00:13:18,423 --> 00:13:21,426
My fingers were swollen,
so I removed it for respite.

178
00:13:22,010 --> 00:13:23,261
[sighs]

179
00:13:23,344 --> 00:13:25,930
That is a ring of healing.
You should keep it on.

180
00:13:26,889 --> 00:13:28,016
That ring…

181
00:13:28,099 --> 00:13:29,142
It will keep you healthy.

182
00:13:30,518 --> 00:13:31,519
Oh?

183
00:13:31,602 --> 00:13:34,647
When I first met you,
your body was covered in scars.

184
00:13:36,733 --> 00:13:38,109
The ring is enchanted.

185
00:13:38,609 --> 00:13:40,361
Wearing it quickened your healing.

186
00:13:41,154 --> 00:13:42,822
It is a mystical treasure.

187
00:13:42,905 --> 00:13:45,283
An ancient heirloom
of the imperial family.

188
00:13:45,366 --> 00:13:46,451
[Rashta] Mmm.

189
00:13:46,534 --> 00:13:48,077
[footsteps approaching]

190
00:13:50,621 --> 00:13:51,789
Please, Your Majesty…

191
00:13:59,380 --> 00:14:00,465
[Rashta sighs]

192
00:14:00,548 --> 00:14:03,134
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

193
00:14:09,974 --> 00:14:11,476
[clicking]

194
00:14:19,358 --> 00:14:20,485
[banging on door]

195
00:14:25,907 --> 00:14:27,366
[Lotteshu's servant] What do you want?

196
00:14:38,586 --> 00:14:39,754
Who?

197
00:14:41,422 --> 00:14:42,548
Why?

198
00:14:43,132 --> 00:14:45,676
I have been sent
to collect something urgently.

199
00:14:46,427 --> 00:14:47,470
What?

200
00:14:48,012 --> 00:14:49,806
The ring with the crimson gemstone.

201
00:14:51,432 --> 00:14:54,018
-Ah…
-I was ordered to bring the ring back.

202
00:14:54,102 --> 00:14:55,436
I'm afraid it's gone.

203
00:14:56,020 --> 00:14:57,021
I'm sorry?

204
00:14:57,605 --> 00:14:58,606
May have sold it.

205
00:14:59,607 --> 00:15:00,775
[gasps] Oh no!

206
00:15:01,859 --> 00:15:03,444
You have to find it right away.

207
00:15:03,528 --> 00:15:06,364
If you cannot find that ring,
then we will all be killed.

208
00:15:06,447 --> 00:15:08,866
The Emperor has been asking after it.

209
00:15:12,120 --> 00:15:13,663
Are you saying he knows about it?

210
00:15:13,746 --> 00:15:16,541
He has told Lady Rashta
that she has to wear it all the time now.

211
00:15:16,624 --> 00:15:19,252
If it is revealed that you took it,
then Rashta,

212
00:15:19,335 --> 00:15:21,170
you and me also…

213
00:15:21,629 --> 00:15:23,673
We will all be dead. Do you understand?

214
00:15:24,924 --> 00:15:25,925
Wait there, girl.

215
00:15:26,008 --> 00:15:27,009
I'll be right back.

216
00:15:28,302 --> 00:15:30,179
[♪ tense music playing]

217
00:15:31,430 --> 00:15:32,598
[grunts in frustration]

218
00:15:41,482 --> 00:15:42,567
[sighs]

219
00:16:16,225 --> 00:16:17,268
[cup clatters]

220
00:16:26,777 --> 00:16:27,945
[♪ music fades]

221
00:16:32,116 --> 00:16:33,117
[sighs]

222
00:16:35,995 --> 00:16:37,205
[Falhan] You have to eat something.

223
00:16:37,288 --> 00:16:38,998
At this rate, you'll starve yourself.

224
00:16:42,501 --> 00:16:43,586
[chair scraping]

225
00:16:44,545 --> 00:16:46,505
PAWNSHOP
THIS MONTH'S AUCTION ITEMS LIST

226
00:16:47,506 --> 00:16:48,633
What's this?

227
00:16:48,716 --> 00:16:50,218
It's from the auction house
across the street.

228
00:16:50,301 --> 00:16:52,261
This is the list of items for sale.

229
00:16:52,345 --> 00:16:55,806
It has something on there
I think you'll find very interesting.

230
00:16:55,890 --> 00:16:57,433
[♪ curious music playing]

231
00:16:59,894 --> 00:17:02,688
[Kosair] Is this not the Emperor's ring?

232
00:17:03,522 --> 00:17:04,732
The crimson stone?

233
00:17:06,609 --> 00:17:08,444
Listed at the pawn shop for sale?

234
00:17:08,986 --> 00:17:09,987
[gasps softly]

235
00:17:21,999 --> 00:17:23,209
Open the door.

236
00:17:23,292 --> 00:17:25,086
Are you there? Open the door!

237
00:17:26,671 --> 00:17:27,797
Open up, hurry!

238
00:17:27,880 --> 00:17:29,966
[shop owner] There must be
something in the air tonight.

239
00:17:30,800 --> 00:17:32,510
We're closed now. You'll have to--

240
00:17:33,052 --> 00:17:34,470
Oh… Viscount.

241
00:17:34,554 --> 00:17:36,806
I need the item I sold to you
for the auction.

242
00:17:36,889 --> 00:17:37,890
Quickly.

243
00:17:37,974 --> 00:17:39,058
Uh… You see…

244
00:17:39,684 --> 00:17:41,269
-Um…
-What?

245
00:17:41,936 --> 00:17:42,979
Where is it?

246
00:17:44,230 --> 00:17:45,606
[Kosair] Looking for this?

247
00:17:47,692 --> 00:17:49,235
[shop owner]
That's the man you need to talk to.

248
00:17:49,318 --> 00:17:51,612
Ah, you already sold it. [sighs]

249
00:17:54,532 --> 00:17:55,741
[exhales deeply]

250
00:17:57,743 --> 00:18:00,204
I've decided I won't be selling the ring.

251
00:18:00,288 --> 00:18:02,582
So you really ought to return it.

252
00:18:03,583 --> 00:18:05,501
The price has gone up a fair bit.

253
00:18:07,461 --> 00:18:09,422
I do hope we can strike a deal.

254
00:18:09,505 --> 00:18:10,506
[Lotteshu] A deal?

255
00:18:11,215 --> 00:18:12,341
[chuckles scornfully]

256
00:18:12,425 --> 00:18:13,467
Ah…

257
00:18:14,135 --> 00:18:16,095
Ah, you must be an outsider.

258
00:18:17,513 --> 00:18:19,348
I am Lotteshu. It's nice to meet you.

259
00:18:20,016 --> 00:18:21,392
If you were from around here,

260
00:18:21,475 --> 00:18:23,519
you would have
heard my name at least once.

261
00:18:24,687 --> 00:18:26,480
Anyway, it's not important.

262
00:18:26,564 --> 00:18:28,107
This is urgent.

263
00:18:28,190 --> 00:18:29,442
So how about--

264
00:18:29,525 --> 00:18:31,193
[both grunt]

265
00:18:32,695 --> 00:18:34,113
I am aware of you.

266
00:18:34,655 --> 00:18:35,656
And you…

267
00:18:36,157 --> 00:18:37,533
will have heard the name Kosair.

268
00:18:37,617 --> 00:18:38,951
Kosair?

269
00:18:39,869 --> 00:18:40,995
The iron-blooded?

270
00:18:44,123 --> 00:18:46,542
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

271
00:19:09,231 --> 00:19:11,067
Five thousand to kill him.

272
00:19:13,319 --> 00:19:14,403
Ten thousand…

273
00:19:15,029 --> 00:19:16,280
if captured alive.

274
00:19:33,047 --> 00:19:34,256
[grunting softly]

275
00:19:39,553 --> 00:19:40,763
[gasps]

276
00:19:43,307 --> 00:19:44,433
[chuckles scornfully]

277
00:19:48,437 --> 00:19:49,438
This ring.

278
00:19:49,522 --> 00:19:52,024
That wench gave it to you, didn't she?

279
00:19:52,108 --> 00:19:54,568
Who is "that wench," sir?

280
00:19:54,652 --> 00:19:58,197
She is now the Emperor's Mistress,
but she was once your slave girl…

281
00:19:58,614 --> 00:19:59,615
Rashta.

282
00:20:00,908 --> 00:20:02,284
Will you not answer?

283
00:20:02,952 --> 00:20:04,161
Yes.

284
00:20:04,245 --> 00:20:05,246
So…

285
00:20:06,163 --> 00:20:07,707
Now you blackmail her.

286
00:20:07,790 --> 00:20:11,836
How did you do it? Threaten her?
To expose her lowly history?

287
00:20:14,380 --> 00:20:16,882
Is that how you're extorting
money from her?

288
00:20:19,385 --> 00:20:20,469
Yes.

289
00:20:20,553 --> 00:20:21,554
That's why.

290
00:20:21,637 --> 00:20:22,847
My lord.

291
00:20:23,389 --> 00:20:24,849
-[Kosair grunts]
-[Lotteshu groans]

292
00:20:25,433 --> 00:20:27,101
[Lotteshu breathing shakily]

293
00:20:27,893 --> 00:20:29,270
It is not wise to lie.

294
00:20:29,353 --> 00:20:31,564
[Lotteshu whimpering]

295
00:20:32,189 --> 00:20:34,608
It is no secret
that Rashta was once a slave.

296
00:20:34,692 --> 00:20:36,527
The Emperor is aware.

297
00:20:37,027 --> 00:20:39,029
How do you plan to use it against her?

298
00:20:40,364 --> 00:20:41,991
Unless that is not all.

299
00:20:42,575 --> 00:20:43,659
Right?

300
00:20:46,412 --> 00:20:48,080
[Lotteshu whimpering]

301
00:20:48,164 --> 00:20:51,000
There is another secret
you and Rashta are withholding

302
00:20:51,083 --> 00:20:54,044
which the Emperor cannot discover
under any circumstances.

303
00:20:55,713 --> 00:20:56,756
Tell me.

304
00:20:57,298 --> 00:20:58,466
[whimpers]

305
00:20:59,341 --> 00:21:01,761
-[exclaims]
-And if you lie again,

306
00:21:02,386 --> 00:21:04,930
then I shall gouge out this eye to match.

307
00:21:06,307 --> 00:21:07,975
All right, all right, all right!

308
00:21:08,058 --> 00:21:10,227
There's a baby, all right? A baby!

309
00:21:10,311 --> 00:21:11,937
She is hiding a baby. Stop…

310
00:21:13,981 --> 00:21:15,107
What?

311
00:21:15,775 --> 00:21:16,776
Say that again.

312
00:21:18,277 --> 00:21:20,488
Rashta had a child before.

313
00:21:23,365 --> 00:21:24,450
[scoffs]

314
00:21:25,576 --> 00:21:26,577
No way.

315
00:21:26,660 --> 00:21:28,621
Who is the father of this baby?

316
00:21:28,704 --> 00:21:32,291
That girl… bewitched my son
with her looks.

317
00:21:34,001 --> 00:21:35,586
[Kosair laughing]

318
00:21:37,296 --> 00:21:40,007
The child that Rashta had…

319
00:21:40,758 --> 00:21:41,884
is your grandchild?

320
00:21:41,967 --> 00:21:43,844
Rashta used him as leverage.

321
00:21:43,928 --> 00:21:45,846
Said my son should wed her for it.

322
00:21:46,514 --> 00:21:49,850
And then she ran away
after I punished her insolence.

323
00:21:50,726 --> 00:21:51,852
[Kosair] So, she ran away…

324
00:21:51,936 --> 00:21:54,021
[♪ tense music playing]

325
00:22:00,152 --> 00:22:01,278
[Kosair sighs]

326
00:22:08,160 --> 00:22:10,079
[Kosair mutters softly]
Rashta, that bitch…

327
00:22:19,588 --> 00:22:20,756
Who's there?

328
00:22:24,051 --> 00:22:25,219
It's me, sir.

329
00:22:25,302 --> 00:22:26,428
Oh.

330
00:22:26,512 --> 00:22:27,513
And who are they?

331
00:22:27,596 --> 00:22:28,931
Charles sent these men.

332
00:22:29,014 --> 00:22:30,057
Charles?

333
00:22:30,140 --> 00:22:32,059
-[door bangs open]
-[gasps]

334
00:22:38,649 --> 00:22:40,985
Why, you sons of bitches! [grunts]

335
00:22:41,068 --> 00:22:42,695
[Kosair yelling]

336
00:22:48,701 --> 00:22:50,077
[exclaiming]

337
00:22:51,537 --> 00:22:54,206
Hey, Kosair! Untie me before you leave!

338
00:22:56,166 --> 00:22:57,209
[grunting]

339
00:23:03,007 --> 00:23:04,884
[Kosair] Be sure to deliver
this ring to the Empress.

340
00:23:04,967 --> 00:23:06,302
And listen, it's about Rashta--

341
00:23:06,385 --> 00:23:07,428
I heard every word.

342
00:23:07,511 --> 00:23:09,430
[chuckles] Excellent.

343
00:23:09,513 --> 00:23:11,140
[Kosair yelling]

344
00:23:11,223 --> 00:23:12,766
[Artina grunting]

345
00:23:36,832 --> 00:23:39,376
You cannot get caught up in this,
or Navier will be in danger.

346
00:23:39,460 --> 00:23:41,337
-Sir, what about you?
-You must leave.

347
00:23:41,837 --> 00:23:43,255
That is an order!

348
00:23:43,339 --> 00:23:44,924
[♪ music swells]

349
00:23:46,467 --> 00:23:47,801
[Kosair yelling]

350
00:23:56,936 --> 00:23:58,270
[♪ music fades]

351
00:24:10,407 --> 00:24:12,660
[muffled] Huh? What's this? Where are we?

352
00:24:12,743 --> 00:24:14,244
Wait! Wait!

353
00:24:16,038 --> 00:24:17,039
Hey, wait a minute!

354
00:24:17,581 --> 00:24:18,582
Where are we going?

355
00:24:18,666 --> 00:24:20,793
Where are you taking us?

356
00:24:20,876 --> 00:24:22,419
Will someone answer me?

357
00:24:22,503 --> 00:24:24,046
Hey, wait. Wait!

358
00:24:24,129 --> 00:24:25,422
[screaming] Where are we going?

359
00:24:28,968 --> 00:24:30,177
[gate closes]

360
00:24:37,017 --> 00:24:38,102
[door opens]

361
00:24:39,395 --> 00:24:40,479
[Heinrey sighs]

362
00:24:42,064 --> 00:24:44,233
Did you not sleep at all last night?

363
00:24:45,901 --> 00:24:47,361
[McKenna continues blowing]

364
00:24:47,444 --> 00:24:49,321
What are you reading
that has you so absorbed?

365
00:24:49,405 --> 00:24:51,156
The list of royal capital,

366
00:24:51,949 --> 00:24:53,701
the deployment of soldiers,

367
00:24:53,784 --> 00:24:55,703
tax collection for the Empire.

368
00:24:55,786 --> 00:24:57,287
[sighs] There's no end.

369
00:24:58,455 --> 00:25:01,583
To think my brother
handled this whilst ill…

370
00:25:04,712 --> 00:25:06,588
So, what are you going to do…

371
00:25:08,674 --> 00:25:10,509
regarding Lady Krista?

372
00:25:16,473 --> 00:25:18,976
You mentioned that you plan
to stand against the council.

373
00:25:21,145 --> 00:25:23,439
The nobles have somehow
already begun treating

374
00:25:23,522 --> 00:25:26,233
the marriage between
the two of you as a guarantee.

375
00:25:26,817 --> 00:25:28,152
What do you think?

376
00:25:28,235 --> 00:25:29,236
[McKenna] Me?

377
00:25:30,446 --> 00:25:34,992
Well, Your Majesty, I plan to stick by you
whatever you decide.

378
00:25:36,326 --> 00:25:38,328
As I have always done and always will.

379
00:25:38,412 --> 00:25:41,957
Even if I stand against everyone else,
and get chased out of the kingdom?

380
00:25:42,041 --> 00:25:45,085
Well then, I shall be chased off
with you, Your Majesty.

381
00:25:45,169 --> 00:25:47,504
Who is the one person
who will devote his loyalty to you,

382
00:25:47,588 --> 00:25:49,882
and remain by your side until the end?

383
00:25:50,466 --> 00:25:51,550
It is me, McKenna.

384
00:25:56,430 --> 00:25:57,848
Is that true for everything?

385
00:25:59,475 --> 00:26:00,601
My one condition…

386
00:26:00,684 --> 00:26:02,352
[♪ melancholy music playing]

387
00:26:02,436 --> 00:26:03,854
It cannot be Navier.

388
00:26:04,563 --> 00:26:05,981
As long as it is not her,

389
00:26:06,607 --> 00:26:08,776
I will support you no matter whom
you take as your wife.

390
00:26:09,443 --> 00:26:10,736
And now you know.

391
00:26:11,487 --> 00:26:12,488
I am with you.

392
00:26:19,745 --> 00:26:20,788
McKenna.

393
00:26:22,414 --> 00:26:23,707
Yes, Sire?

394
00:26:24,583 --> 00:26:25,876
You know what?

395
00:26:26,919 --> 00:26:28,295
I miss her terribly.

396
00:26:32,841 --> 00:26:34,051
The rising sun…

397
00:26:35,594 --> 00:26:37,304
the blushing pink of sunset…

398
00:26:39,306 --> 00:26:40,599
When I open my eyes

399
00:26:41,183 --> 00:26:42,434
and when I close them.

400
00:26:43,977 --> 00:26:45,229
Every flower.

401
00:26:45,854 --> 00:26:47,314
The soft glow of the moon.

402
00:26:49,608 --> 00:26:51,485
Any beauty in this world…

403
00:26:53,028 --> 00:26:54,738
brings thoughts of Navier.

404
00:26:57,157 --> 00:26:58,992
I am powerless to it.

405
00:27:00,494 --> 00:27:01,995
Glimpses are everywhere.

406
00:27:03,122 --> 00:27:04,123
Her fragrance…

407
00:27:12,840 --> 00:27:14,800
[♪ music continues]

408
00:27:22,558 --> 00:27:24,309
[♪ music swells]

409
00:27:38,615 --> 00:27:40,158
[birds chirping]

410
00:27:47,916 --> 00:27:49,918
[♪ music fades]

411
00:27:51,962 --> 00:27:53,005
[door opens]

412
00:27:58,594 --> 00:27:59,928
Is there any news?

413
00:28:00,470 --> 00:28:02,139
Has Artina sent word?

414
00:28:02,222 --> 00:28:04,433
No. Nothing yet, Your Majesty.

415
00:28:15,235 --> 00:28:16,361
Kosair did that?

416
00:28:16,445 --> 00:28:17,571
[Albani] Yes, Your Majesty.

417
00:28:17,654 --> 00:28:19,948
He beat and tortured Viscount Lotteshu.

418
00:28:20,032 --> 00:28:22,534
And demanded that he reveal
Ms. Rashta's weakness.

419
00:28:23,201 --> 00:28:24,912
[sighs] Rashta's weakness…

420
00:28:24,995 --> 00:28:26,705
He desired to find evidence

421
00:28:26,788 --> 00:28:29,833
that Rashta was indeed
Viscount Lotteshu's slave.

422
00:28:29,917 --> 00:28:31,501
-[Sovieshu scoffs]
-Your Majesty,

423
00:28:31,585 --> 00:28:34,713
it is clear to me that he wants
to tarnish your child's name.

424
00:28:34,796 --> 00:28:38,884
To shackle the unborn babe
with its mother's lowly past status.

425
00:28:38,967 --> 00:28:40,594
You cannot ignore this.

426
00:28:40,677 --> 00:28:42,888
Kosair will never stop, Your Majesty.

427
00:28:42,971 --> 00:28:45,682
I know in my heart that that man,
he wants to…

428
00:28:46,642 --> 00:28:48,310
He wants to harm your child.

429
00:28:49,061 --> 00:28:50,145
[grunts angrily]

430
00:28:50,228 --> 00:28:52,397
That son of a…

431
00:28:52,481 --> 00:28:53,732
Please…

432
00:28:54,441 --> 00:28:56,568
You must defend the child, Your Majesty.

433
00:28:57,277 --> 00:29:00,155
Even though the baby
borrowed the womb of a mistress,

434
00:29:00,238 --> 00:29:02,199
it is your royal flesh and blood.

435
00:29:02,282 --> 00:29:03,784
I have to wonder…

436
00:29:04,493 --> 00:29:07,996
whether this child
is Your Majesty's last opportunity

437
00:29:08,914 --> 00:29:10,749
for a royal heir?

438
00:29:15,420 --> 00:29:16,797
Explain yourself.

439
00:29:18,799 --> 00:29:19,967
The Empress is…

440
00:29:20,842 --> 00:29:22,803
She is not capable of bearing children.

441
00:29:28,600 --> 00:29:29,851
[gasps]

442
00:29:29,935 --> 00:29:32,729
I… apologize.
Were you not aware, Your Majesty?

443
00:29:32,813 --> 00:29:35,357
[♪ tense music playing]

444
00:29:35,440 --> 00:29:36,817
These allegations…

445
00:29:38,777 --> 00:29:40,278
Do you even have any grounds?

446
00:29:40,362 --> 00:29:42,030
[gasps] Good heavens!

447
00:29:44,783 --> 00:29:46,284
When you were children,

448
00:29:46,368 --> 00:29:48,120
there was an incident, Your Majesty.

449
00:29:48,787 --> 00:29:51,623
The previous empress
was hosting a tea party.

450
00:29:51,707 --> 00:29:52,958
The two of you were playing,

451
00:29:53,041 --> 00:29:55,961
and I caught you stealing
and eating cookies from the spread.

452
00:29:56,044 --> 00:29:57,337
Do you remember?

453
00:29:57,421 --> 00:29:58,755
[both giggling]

454
00:29:58,839 --> 00:30:00,048
[Albani gasps]

455
00:30:00,132 --> 00:30:02,801
-Did you two eat something?
-[both laughing]

456
00:30:05,846 --> 00:30:07,264
[gasping softly]

457
00:30:13,061 --> 00:30:14,187
Cookies?

458
00:30:14,271 --> 00:30:16,481
Not a single one
of your predecessor's mistresses

459
00:30:16,565 --> 00:30:17,607
could bear children.

460
00:30:18,316 --> 00:30:20,610
Did you believe that was a coincidence?

461
00:30:21,236 --> 00:30:22,446
No, Your Majesty.

462
00:30:22,529 --> 00:30:24,740
It was orchestrated
by the previous empress.

463
00:30:24,823 --> 00:30:26,366
Each of these eight mistresses

464
00:30:26,450 --> 00:30:28,785
was to eat one of these cookies,
Your Majesty.

465
00:30:30,370 --> 00:30:31,705
There is no antidote.

466
00:30:32,247 --> 00:30:33,874
She made every one infertile.

467
00:30:36,334 --> 00:30:38,420
-Pardon?
-You hear right, Your Majesty.

468
00:30:38,503 --> 00:30:40,464
Once you've eaten them,
you cannot conceive.

469
00:30:40,547 --> 00:30:43,508
And if someone is pregnant,
it causes them to miscarry.

470
00:30:50,098 --> 00:30:51,266
[Sovieshu exhales deeply]

471
00:30:57,314 --> 00:31:00,859
Why did you hide this secret until now?

472
00:31:03,403 --> 00:31:05,280
Did you think if I was childless…

473
00:31:06,323 --> 00:31:09,951
then your own descendant
would have a chance to take over?

474
00:31:10,035 --> 00:31:12,704
Your Majesty, that is not true!
How could you think that of me?

475
00:31:13,622 --> 00:31:16,083
I could never commit
such an act of disloyalty!

476
00:31:17,292 --> 00:31:18,376
It is because of…

477
00:31:18,960 --> 00:31:19,961
a promise.

478
00:31:20,045 --> 00:31:22,839
The previous empress
asked that I take this to the grave.

479
00:31:22,923 --> 00:31:24,216
I had to.

480
00:31:24,299 --> 00:31:25,926
I had to keep my promise to her.

481
00:31:26,009 --> 00:31:27,010
[shushing]

482
00:31:32,224 --> 00:31:33,433
A promise?

483
00:31:37,145 --> 00:31:39,356
Is that what it was?

484
00:31:41,691 --> 00:31:42,692
[Albani groans]

485
00:31:42,776 --> 00:31:44,277
Did you find it amusing

486
00:31:45,153 --> 00:31:49,991
to watch the Empress and I
struggle desperately to have a child

487
00:31:50,075 --> 00:31:52,202
all because of a promise?

488
00:31:52,285 --> 00:31:54,913
[straining] I was relieved Your Majesty
was unaffected.

489
00:31:54,996 --> 00:31:57,165
I mean that sincerely. I really do.

490
00:31:57,249 --> 00:31:58,875
[gasping for air]

491
00:31:58,959 --> 00:32:01,711
[straining] How could I possibly
have told you this?

492
00:32:02,546 --> 00:32:04,965
Oh, how it has plagued my heart!

493
00:32:07,551 --> 00:32:09,886
-[Sovieshu grunts]
-[Albani gasping for air]

494
00:32:12,639 --> 00:32:14,599
[both panting]

495
00:32:22,941 --> 00:32:24,401
It can be said with certainty

496
00:32:25,527 --> 00:32:28,822
that Her Majesty was
the only one affected by infertility.

497
00:32:30,407 --> 00:32:32,242
[exhales] Rashta's own pregnancy…

498
00:32:33,285 --> 00:32:35,328
It proves that very fact, Your Majesty!

499
00:32:35,412 --> 00:32:36,538
[breathing shakily]

500
00:32:37,205 --> 00:32:38,206
Lante!

501
00:32:42,377 --> 00:32:43,378
Your Majesty?

502
00:32:45,755 --> 00:32:47,549
Confine Kosair.

503
00:32:47,632 --> 00:32:51,094
Send the knights immediately
and have him locked in Charles' farmhouse.

504
00:32:51,761 --> 00:32:53,597
We cannot have him wandering around.

505
00:32:54,306 --> 00:32:56,391
We must isolate him entirely…

506
00:32:57,184 --> 00:32:58,977
so he cannot contact anyone.

507
00:33:00,312 --> 00:33:01,730
[Sovieshu panting]

508
00:33:04,774 --> 00:33:06,526
[♪ music intensifies]

509
00:33:11,698 --> 00:33:12,782
Leave now.

510
00:33:24,753 --> 00:33:25,754
[door closes]

511
00:33:48,360 --> 00:33:50,528
[Albani] <i>Not a single one</i>
<i>of your predecessor's mistresses</i>

512
00:33:50,612 --> 00:33:51,613
<i>could bear children.</i>

513
00:33:52,572 --> 00:33:55,367
<i>Did you believe that was a coincidence?</i>

514
00:33:55,450 --> 00:33:56,534
<i>No, Your Majesty.</i>

515
00:33:56,618 --> 00:33:58,703
<i>It was orchestrated</i>
<i>by the previous empress.</i>

516
00:33:59,829 --> 00:34:01,915
There is no antidote.

517
00:34:01,998 --> 00:34:03,583
She made everyone infertile.

518
00:34:06,044 --> 00:34:07,087
[exhales deeply]

519
00:34:10,840 --> 00:34:11,883
[door closes]

520
00:34:11,967 --> 00:34:13,051
Is it done?

521
00:34:14,719 --> 00:34:17,013
-Have you completed the review?
-[Count Norayu] Yes, Your Majesty.

522
00:34:17,097 --> 00:34:19,683
We thoroughly scoured records
of past reigns

523
00:34:19,766 --> 00:34:21,601
and all the books on royal law.

524
00:34:21,685 --> 00:34:25,730
But no child born to a mistress
can rise to the position of imperial heir.

525
00:34:25,814 --> 00:34:27,148
There is no precedent.

526
00:34:27,232 --> 00:34:31,987
Only Her Majesty the Empress' child
can inherit the imperial throne.

527
00:34:41,496 --> 00:34:44,499
Have you seen the delegation list
being prepared by the Duchy of Baltin?

528
00:34:44,582 --> 00:34:45,583
Not yet.

529
00:34:45,667 --> 00:34:48,336
You know, there are a good few
wealthy merchants on there.

530
00:34:48,420 --> 00:34:50,213
They'll want
the Western Kingdom's rare minerals

531
00:34:50,297 --> 00:34:52,340
and will haggle for the lowest price.

532
00:34:52,424 --> 00:34:54,009
To profit from the situation.

533
00:34:54,092 --> 00:34:56,511
Uh, shall we also include merchants?

534
00:34:58,179 --> 00:34:59,639
[door opens]

535
00:35:02,517 --> 00:35:04,853
[softly] Sir Artina
has returned to the palace.

536
00:35:04,936 --> 00:35:06,605
He wants to see Your Majesty urgently.

537
00:35:13,570 --> 00:35:15,030
[Artina grunts in pain]

538
00:35:15,113 --> 00:35:16,364
Artina, you're bleeding!

539
00:35:17,324 --> 00:35:19,075
-Call the physician.
-Your Majesty…

540
00:35:19,159 --> 00:35:20,535
I bear important news.

541
00:35:21,870 --> 00:35:23,872
Sir Kosair is in peril.

542
00:35:25,040 --> 00:35:26,041
What's happened?

543
00:35:26,708 --> 00:35:29,252
He said to give this to you.

544
00:35:37,385 --> 00:35:38,887
It is Rashta.

545
00:35:38,970 --> 00:35:40,221
She is already a mother.

546
00:35:42,265 --> 00:35:44,267
[gasps] There's another child?

547
00:35:44,809 --> 00:35:46,603
Lotteshu's son is the father.

548
00:35:46,686 --> 00:35:48,647
-They had a child together.
-[♪ ominous music playing]

549
00:35:48,730 --> 00:35:51,191
It is a newborn,
about five to six months old.

550
00:36:02,702 --> 00:36:05,205
[Eliza] Why do you hesitate, Your Majesty?

551
00:36:05,288 --> 00:36:09,334
The Albani House and Miss Rashta
colluded together to deceive His Majesty.

552
00:36:09,417 --> 00:36:11,503
You have to tell him the whole truth.

553
00:36:13,129 --> 00:36:14,798
It will save Sir Kosair.

554
00:36:19,302 --> 00:36:21,262
If his knights arrived on his orders,

555
00:36:22,222 --> 00:36:23,682
His Majesty must know.

556
00:36:24,349 --> 00:36:26,476
Surely, he knows everything already.

557
00:36:30,939 --> 00:36:32,315
I am left with no choice.

558
00:36:33,024 --> 00:36:34,776
I will speak to His Majesty

559
00:36:34,859 --> 00:36:36,236
and I will save my brother.

560
00:36:48,164 --> 00:36:50,125
[♪ tense music playing]

561
00:36:51,876 --> 00:36:53,211
[door opens]

562
00:36:54,421 --> 00:36:55,505
[door closes]

563
00:37:01,720 --> 00:37:05,557
I have carried out everything
as Your Majesty instructed, but I…

564
00:37:06,766 --> 00:37:08,143
[Sovieshu sighs]

565
00:37:08,226 --> 00:37:09,436
[Sovieshu] Lante.

566
00:37:10,854 --> 00:37:12,021
[Marquess Lante] Yes, Your Majesty?

567
00:37:18,611 --> 00:37:20,572
[♪ melancholy music playing]

568
00:37:20,655 --> 00:37:22,031
The Empress…

569
00:37:30,206 --> 00:37:31,666
I have to divorce her.

570
00:37:39,716 --> 00:37:41,718
[♪ dramatic music playing]

571
00:37:51,561 --> 00:37:52,729
[Annie] Your Majesty.

572
00:38:15,668 --> 00:38:17,086
[♪ music fades]

573
00:38:51,162 --> 00:38:52,455
[Rashta] What are you saying?

574
00:38:56,000 --> 00:38:57,377
What do you mean, a divorce?

575
00:38:58,545 --> 00:38:59,796
[Sovieshu] Exactly that.

576
00:39:00,797 --> 00:39:02,507
I mean to divorce the Empress.

577
00:39:03,925 --> 00:39:05,093
[Rashta] Why?

578
00:39:06,010 --> 00:39:07,095
So…

579
00:39:07,595 --> 00:39:09,347
So what is going to happen next?

580
00:39:22,944 --> 00:39:24,571
You will become the empress.

581
00:39:30,243 --> 00:39:31,411
Ah…

582
00:39:31,953 --> 00:39:33,997
The Empress will not choose to step aside.

583
00:39:34,873 --> 00:39:37,125
I know she will not take
a divorce lightly.

584
00:39:38,084 --> 00:39:40,086
Her family could create issues, too.

585
00:39:40,169 --> 00:39:42,630
Hmm. I do not think so.

586
00:39:42,714 --> 00:39:44,340
So, what will you do?

587
00:39:46,259 --> 00:39:47,427
I'll take care of it.

588
00:39:49,178 --> 00:39:50,179
So do not worry.

589
00:39:53,892 --> 00:39:55,435
I will do what I can.

590
00:39:58,605 --> 00:40:02,317
[Sovieshu] You need only devote yourself
to keeping your body healthy.

591
00:40:04,360 --> 00:40:07,697
And until I say, keep what
we discussed today between us.

592
00:40:07,780 --> 00:40:09,490
[♪ sad, heartfelt music playing]

593
00:40:15,413 --> 00:40:16,748
[door closes]

594
00:40:40,146 --> 00:40:41,856
[breathes heavily]

595
00:40:45,109 --> 00:40:47,111
[♪ music intensifies]

596
00:41:17,016 --> 00:41:18,059
Is it really true?

597
00:41:22,814 --> 00:41:24,440
I'm to become the empress?

598
00:41:28,861 --> 00:41:30,863
[snorts, laughing]

599
00:41:36,911 --> 00:41:37,996
Rashta!

600
00:41:40,498 --> 00:41:41,624
The Empress.

601
00:41:45,378 --> 00:41:46,379
[exhales]

602
00:41:47,338 --> 00:41:49,257
Rashta, the new Empress.

603
00:41:50,633 --> 00:41:51,634
Rashta…

604
00:41:52,552 --> 00:41:53,553
Ishka…

605
00:41:55,054 --> 00:41:56,180
Botulin.

606
00:41:56,264 --> 00:41:58,099
[♪ grand music playing]

607
00:42:03,855 --> 00:42:05,606
[♪ music continues]

608
00:42:12,780 --> 00:42:14,032
[birds chirping]

609
00:42:22,957 --> 00:42:25,209
[Heinrey] <i>What usually happens</i>
<i>to a widowed queen?</i>

610
00:42:25,293 --> 00:42:28,337
She would vacate the palace
and move to an estate in Compshire.

611
00:42:28,421 --> 00:42:29,756
There is no formal decree,

612
00:42:29,839 --> 00:42:31,841
but that is what I learned
from our records.

613
00:42:31,924 --> 00:42:33,384
Find those records.

614
00:42:33,468 --> 00:42:34,677
Yes, Your Majesty.

615
00:42:34,761 --> 00:42:35,762
[birds chirping]

616
00:42:40,808 --> 00:42:41,809
[Krista] Heinrey.

617
00:42:45,229 --> 00:42:46,898
Shall we walk together?

618
00:42:47,690 --> 00:42:49,025
Just like we used to…

619
00:42:49,734 --> 00:42:51,360
when we were children.

620
00:42:53,071 --> 00:42:54,697
[♪ soft music playing]

621
00:42:54,781 --> 00:42:56,199
When we were children?

622
00:42:56,783 --> 00:42:57,992
[Krista] Mmm.

623
00:42:59,827 --> 00:43:02,246
Are you accustomed
to life at the palace yet?

624
00:43:02,789 --> 00:43:05,249
I wonder if it's because I was born here,

625
00:43:05,333 --> 00:43:07,001
the palace has embraced me quickly.

626
00:43:07,085 --> 00:43:10,338
The people, however,
do not acknowledge me at all.

627
00:43:11,839 --> 00:43:14,634
The Council of Elders
may be rather territorial.

628
00:43:14,717 --> 00:43:16,344
If you yield on the tax issue,

629
00:43:16,427 --> 00:43:18,513
many others will be resolved easily.

630
00:43:18,596 --> 00:43:21,766
You should be selective
of your battles with them.

631
00:43:21,849 --> 00:43:25,103
You must be careful and do not fall
into the trap Father left you.

632
00:43:25,186 --> 00:43:26,562
You should have patience…

633
00:43:27,563 --> 00:43:28,898
and forge a path of your own.

634
00:43:30,066 --> 00:43:32,652
You asked to go for a walk
like we used to,

635
00:43:32,735 --> 00:43:34,403
but I suspect there's another reason.

636
00:43:35,279 --> 00:43:36,364
That may be the case.

637
00:43:36,447 --> 00:43:38,950
Besides, some Elders value
the new king's drive.

638
00:43:39,033 --> 00:43:40,785
[Heinrey chuckles]

639
00:43:40,868 --> 00:43:42,537
You have changed.

640
00:43:43,412 --> 00:43:46,666
The power struggle between Father
and the late king was rife.

641
00:43:46,749 --> 00:43:48,000
I heard as such.

642
00:43:48,084 --> 00:43:50,628
My brother had you.
Your solidarity was useful to him.

643
00:43:52,421 --> 00:43:54,006
You can also use me.

644
00:43:54,632 --> 00:43:56,759
I can give strength to your voice.

645
00:43:58,219 --> 00:44:00,179
That option is there for you.

646
00:44:01,389 --> 00:44:02,431
Krista…

647
00:44:09,730 --> 00:44:11,858
Everyone has an opinion on our marriage,

648
00:44:11,941 --> 00:44:13,151
but not us.

649
00:44:13,234 --> 00:44:15,444
As we have not yet had the chance to talk.

650
00:44:17,155 --> 00:44:19,115
Royal marriages often work that way.

651
00:44:20,199 --> 00:44:22,368
A political contract is all this is.

652
00:44:22,451 --> 00:44:23,786
Our wishes are secondary.

653
00:44:25,580 --> 00:44:27,999
Our unity is a safe choice

654
00:44:28,082 --> 00:44:29,458
and a political one.

655
00:44:29,542 --> 00:44:31,377
But do you not wish for love?

656
00:44:31,460 --> 00:44:34,422
I also wish to serve the people,
not just the Council of Elders.

657
00:44:34,505 --> 00:44:36,674
We are in a position
to change how things are.

658
00:44:36,757 --> 00:44:38,551
The kingdom deserves a new start.

659
00:44:39,427 --> 00:44:41,220
One that I know will make us proud.

660
00:44:41,304 --> 00:44:43,639
Your thoughts on royal marriage are sound.

661
00:44:43,723 --> 00:44:45,308
Is there a lady you think of?

662
00:44:46,475 --> 00:44:47,476
Is there?

663
00:44:47,560 --> 00:44:49,020
[♪ gentle music playing]

664
00:44:53,316 --> 00:44:54,650
Yes, there is someone.

665
00:44:55,776 --> 00:44:56,986
She's the one.

666
00:45:12,835 --> 00:45:15,421
[Eliza] I heard
there was a frost overnight,

667
00:45:16,672 --> 00:45:19,383
but now the weather has grown warm again.

668
00:45:23,888 --> 00:45:25,473
Have you discussed the issue…

669
00:45:26,057 --> 00:45:28,142
with Rashta? Or with His Majesty?

670
00:45:29,143 --> 00:45:30,728
What did he say?

671
00:45:30,811 --> 00:45:32,605
I did not speak to him.

672
00:45:35,691 --> 00:45:36,692
Countess Eliza…

673
00:45:38,194 --> 00:45:39,403
You said Rashta…

674
00:45:40,071 --> 00:45:42,198
will be taught by the finest of teachers?

675
00:45:42,281 --> 00:45:43,491
Yes.

676
00:45:43,574 --> 00:45:47,536
I heard His Majesty
had personally selected all the tutors,

677
00:45:47,620 --> 00:45:48,871
some of whom were yours.

678
00:45:50,373 --> 00:45:54,252
Rashta will be learning
everything that all the nobles do.

679
00:45:54,335 --> 00:45:57,588
Her tutorage will start at the basics,
like any highborn child.

680
00:45:57,672 --> 00:45:59,715
She must memorize
all of the state officials,

681
00:46:00,424 --> 00:46:01,425
the nobles…

682
00:46:01,968 --> 00:46:04,178
and the Imperial history and family tree.

683
00:46:04,262 --> 00:46:06,806
And when was this education initiated?

684
00:46:08,015 --> 00:46:09,433
After she fell pregnant.

685
00:46:10,476 --> 00:46:11,936
After she fell pregnant?

686
00:46:18,025 --> 00:46:19,527
Your Majesty,

687
00:46:19,610 --> 00:46:21,279
this evening with His Majesty
is scheduled.

688
00:46:21,362 --> 00:46:24,240
You are set to have dinner
with His Majesty, as usual.

689
00:46:24,824 --> 00:46:26,117
What outfit should I prepare?

690
00:46:28,744 --> 00:46:30,037
I would like a colorful one.

691
00:46:30,830 --> 00:46:32,331
-We will prepare it.
-We will prepare it.

692
00:46:40,589 --> 00:46:42,591
[♪ tense music playing]

693
00:46:51,017 --> 00:46:53,686
My brother is confined
under Your Majesty's orders.

694
00:46:54,562 --> 00:46:55,813
When will he be freed?

695
00:47:06,657 --> 00:47:08,701
How did you come across that knowledge?

696
00:47:08,784 --> 00:47:11,787
How could you forget that
the walls have ears in this palace?

697
00:47:12,788 --> 00:47:14,623
I am aware of everything.

698
00:47:15,207 --> 00:47:16,751
I am the Empress.

699
00:47:20,546 --> 00:47:22,882
If you heard that your brother
is in confinement…

700
00:47:24,216 --> 00:47:27,094
Then I assume… you know why.

701
00:47:27,720 --> 00:47:31,640
He sought gossip about Rashta,
and in doing so reduced an innocent man…

702
00:47:32,350 --> 00:47:33,934
to a bloody mess.

703
00:47:35,728 --> 00:47:37,480
You call him an innocent man.

704
00:47:38,522 --> 00:47:40,232
Now, tell me, sire.

705
00:47:40,316 --> 00:47:43,194
Is this innocent man
the one whose eye you removed?

706
00:47:43,903 --> 00:47:45,738
Did you not make him swear to you

707
00:47:46,655 --> 00:47:48,616
that he would never speak of Rashta again?

708
00:47:53,079 --> 00:47:54,413
I warned you of this.

709
00:47:54,497 --> 00:47:55,581
[sniffs]

710
00:47:56,499 --> 00:47:59,627
I will protect my unborn child
at all costs.

711
00:47:59,710 --> 00:48:01,962
And that includes
when Rashta is threatened.

712
00:48:13,891 --> 00:48:15,476
The decision is made.

713
00:48:16,769 --> 00:48:18,771
General Kosair is banished.

714
00:48:18,854 --> 00:48:20,147
You don't mean that.

715
00:48:20,856 --> 00:48:22,483
Clearly, I can no longer trust him.

716
00:48:22,566 --> 00:48:26,070
And I think that
even you cannot control him now.

717
00:48:27,613 --> 00:48:30,241
And I am not convinced
that that will change.

718
00:48:32,660 --> 00:48:34,745
My brother's efforts were not in vain.

719
00:48:36,372 --> 00:48:38,249
Are you even aware of what he obtained?

720
00:48:39,041 --> 00:48:42,670
Yes! He was searching
for Rashta's slave documentation.

721
00:48:43,754 --> 00:48:45,172
Such things do not exist.

722
00:48:46,132 --> 00:48:48,217
Must you have such hatred for her?

723
00:48:48,300 --> 00:48:49,760
That poor, defenseless creature.

724
00:48:49,844 --> 00:48:51,470
She has lived such a pitiful life.

725
00:48:51,554 --> 00:48:54,723
She finally stands tall
with humility and grace.

726
00:48:54,807 --> 00:48:58,519
Yet you are desperate to take it from her,
despite having so much.

727
00:48:58,602 --> 00:49:01,981
That child has no greed, no desire,
no background, and no power.

728
00:49:02,064 --> 00:49:03,691
She cannot compete.

729
00:49:03,774 --> 00:49:05,901
And yet, you are still threatened.

730
00:49:05,985 --> 00:49:07,862
That girl carries my child,

731
00:49:07,945 --> 00:49:11,365
and you and your brother,
members of such an influential family,

732
00:49:12,908 --> 00:49:15,536
want nothing more than to besmirch her.

733
00:49:20,958 --> 00:49:23,419
[laughs scornfully]

734
00:49:30,926 --> 00:49:32,303
[chuckles softly]

735
00:49:39,560 --> 00:49:40,978
[chuckles]

736
00:49:45,399 --> 00:49:46,692
I have no appetite.

737
00:49:48,068 --> 00:49:49,528
It's time for me to depart.

738
00:50:00,331 --> 00:50:02,291
[♪ grand music playing]

739
00:50:05,252 --> 00:50:06,587
The coronation…

740
00:50:07,963 --> 00:50:09,798
I have decided upon the delegate.

741
00:50:13,219 --> 00:50:14,637
I will go.

742
00:50:14,720 --> 00:50:16,347
[♪ music swells]

743
00:50:19,350 --> 00:50:22,520
THE REMARRIED EMPRESS

744
00:50:23,479 --> 00:50:25,481
[♪ closing theme music playing]
